  heroes  html/sanitize.allow_attributes, html/sanitize.EVERY_ELEMENT
  go      Policy.AllowAttrs, attrPolicyBuilder.OnElements, attrPolicyBuilder.Globally
  rust    Builder::tag_attributes, Builder::add_tag_attributes, Builder::generic_attributes, Builder::add_generic_attributes
  python  bleach.clean(attributes=) as a dict or a list, nh3.clean(attributes=)
  note    `*` for every element, as bleach and nh3 write it; the standard's `allowAttribute` and an element's `attributes`. An event handler and `srcdoc` never stay

capability sanitize/attribute-pattern  an attribute kept where a pattern matches its value
  heroes  html/sanitize.allow_attributes_matching
  go      attrPolicyBuilder.Matching
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    `regex` matches the whole value, so a pattern needs no anchors where bluemonday's do

capability sanitize/attribute-values  an attribute kept where its value is one of a list
  heroes  html/sanitize.allow_attribute_values
  go      -
  rust    Builder::tag_attribute_values, Builder::add_tag_attribute_values, Builder::rm_tag_attribute_values
