capability sanitize/attribute-function  an attribute kept where a function of the program accepts its value
  heroes  html/sanitize.allow_attributes_where
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  bleach.clean(attributes=) as a function, bleach.sanitizer.attribute_filter_factory
  note    a top-level function of the program, the language having no closure

capability sanitize/attribute-filter  every attribute kept rewritten or taken out by a function of the program
  heroes  html/sanitize.filter_attributes
  go      Policy.RewriteSrc
  rust    Builder::attribute_filter, AttributeFilter, UrlRelative::Custom, UrlRelativeEvaluate, Builder::is_url_relative_custom
  python  nh3.clean(attribute_filter=), nh3.clean(url_relative=) as a function
  note    run before the URL, style and class of the attribute are checked, so what it writes is checked as any other value (a test proxies an image's `src` and still refuses it once `https` is forbidden); run on the first reading alone, as a rewrite read again would be rewritten twice

capability sanitize/attribute-prefixes  attributes kept by the beginning of their name
  heroes  html/sanitize.allow_attribute_prefixes
