capability sanitize/id-prefix  every `id` kept prefixed, against DOM clobbering
  heroes  html/sanitize.prefix_ids
  go      -
  rust    Builder::id_prefix
  python  nh3.clean(id_prefix=)
  note    prefixed on the first reading; the readings that check the answer prefix only an `id` that lacks the prefix, so the answer settles. The standard's 8.6.6.2 names DOM clobbering

capability sanitize/styles  the properties of a `style` attribute kept by name, and their values checked
  heroes  html/sanitize.allow_styles, html/sanitize.allow_styles_matching, html/sanitize.allow_style_values, html/sanitize.allow_styles_where
  go      Policy.AllowStyles, stylePolicyBuilder.Globally, stylePolicyBuilder.OnElements, stylePolicyBuilder.Matching, stylePolicyBuilder.MatchingEnum, stylePolicyBuilder.MatchingHandler
  rust    Builder::filter_style_properties
  python  bleach.css_sanitizer.CSSSanitizer, bleach.css_sanitizer.ALLOWED_CSS_PROPERTIES, bleach.css_sanitizer.ALLOWED_SVG_PROPERTIES, bleach.clean(css_sanitizer=), bleach.sanitizer.NoCssSanitizerWarning, nh3.clean(filter_style_properties=)
  note    written again `property: value` joined by `; `, as bluemonday writes it (observed), the property in lower case and `!important` taken off as bluemonday takes it off. A value that calls `url()`, `image-set()`, `expression()` or any function but those of colours, gradients, transforms, filters and arithmetic never stays, nor one with a backslash or a comment: bluemonday keeps `background: url(http://...)` and nh3 keeps `color: url("x")` (observed), which load what the author of the fragment chooses. No ready list of properties as bleach's: a program names its own

capability sanitize/url-schemes  the URL schemes kept in every attribute that holds a URL
  heroes  html/sanitize.allow_url_schemes, html/sanitize.forbid_url_schemes
