  rust    Builder::url_schemes, Builder::add_url_schemes, Builder::rm_url_schemes
  python  bleach.clean(protocols=), nh3.clean(url_schemes=)
  note    the scheme read as the standard's URL parser reads it (controls and spaces cut, tabs and line breaks taken out), so every spelling of `javascript:` in OWASP's cheat sheet is refused; `javascript` and `vbscript` never stay, the standard's `setJavascriptURLs(false)`. A URL kept is one `url.parse_loose` reads, as bluemonday's `RequireParseableURLs`; it is written in the form the browser reads

