dropped
  go      Query, Query.Key, Query.Value, Query.HasValue: a part of a query string, which `url.parse_query` reads as `url.Pair`
  rust    Builder::clone_tags, Builder::clone_clean_content_tags, Builder::clone_tag_attributes, Builder::clone_tag_attribute_values, Builder::clone_set_tag_attribute_values, Builder::clone_generic_attributes, Builder::clone_generic_attribute_prefixes, Builder::clone_url_schemes, Builder::clone_allowed_classes, Builder::get_set_tag_attribute_value: a builder's sets read back or copied; a policy is a value the program built, copied by `=`
  rust    Builder::borrow, Builder::borrow_mut, Builder::fmt, Builder::from, Builder::into, Builder::try_from, Builder::try_into, Builder::type_id: traits of Rust's, which the language has no form for
  rust    Url: the `url` crate's type, re-exported; `url.Url` here
  python  bleach.html5lib_shim, bleach.parse_shim, bleach.six_shim, bleach.sanitizer, bleach.css_sanitizer, nh3.nh3: the modules that carry the names above, and the vendored html5lib and six
